  "prompt": "Exact authoring task: create an editable furry Muse-style panda from the new smooth Meshy base, with four restrained meaningful motions, preserving its small green dragon on the anatomical-right/viewer-left shoulder. Source f3b8c6f48222ef2e588ef1798f788a79909a660f5467b92719d2242b7ad47188 was inspected in outputs/muse-panda-smooth-inspection-v1: front, back, normalized front/side guides and native-inspection/preflight. Do not reuse the old coarse-fur geometry or its rig. Preserve all source geometry, UVs and textures: no smoothing, decimation, repainting or remeshing. Uniformly calibrate the complete avatar to an authored 1.2m height, not a measured human height. The raw glTF +Y-up mesh becomes Blender +Z up/-Y front; all authored positions are normalized from its actual single-mesh world bounds.\nAuthor sixteen panda bones: fixed Root/Pelvis and foot controls, Torso/Neck/Head, separate left/right shoulder-upper-arm-forearm-hand chains, and Tail. Use spatial feathered weight layers, keeping the belly out of the free forearm selection and rigid upper-head/foot regions. A seventeenth CompanionAnchor is created once by the existing green-color plus bounded-region attachment pass, parented to the static anatomical-right shoulder; it is intentionally absent from authored_rig.bones. The already bent supporting arm stays neutral in every action. The separate green strip near the rear pelvis is an uncertain generated color artifact: exclude it from the companion attachment and from fur. A separate explicitly bounded material-only correction may address it; no recovered anatomy is claimed. Review attachment boundaries and palm/body separation in actual poses.\nIdle is a tiny upper-body sway and head settling; look_around is a small alternating head turn; wave lifts the free anatomical-left/viewer-right forearm slightly outward with two wrist turns; celebrate is a short free-arm lift with two head nods. Keep root, pelvis and both feet unanimated, no translations, props, finger articulation, jumping or locomotion. Each action spans exactly four seconds and returns to neutral. Loop certification remains false: matching endpoints are not seamless-loop proof.\nApply6500 native parents with30 children, .018m strands, .00017m radius and the carried bounded comb/shader settings; no native-child override. Adapt face exclusions to the new eyes at normalized X .447/.671, Z .741/.733, nose at X .558,Z .673, and the newly observed companion envelope. Short muzzle/eye-neighbor strands, outward cheek flow, lifted crown/ear flow and downward body flow are authored grooming. Use2400 combed-v1 portable cards with actual source-root colors, inherited skin and the same regional flow. Native hair and portable cards remain different representations. Set texture-normal strength .15, 1024px/48 samples and raw portrait denoising false; framing favors the shoulder companion. Validate actual native and exported appearance/motion separately before quality acceptance. This is not original Muse reconstruction, verified Muse parity, physical animation or a frozen-profile Weft conversion. Local authored correction: only green-dominant rear-tail-base faces inside a tight rear-pelvis ellipsoid become matte charcoal. Shoulder companion greens stay unchanged. Corrected tail-base faces are deliberately excluded from fur; source textures and geometry remain unchanged, and hidden-tail shape remains a generated assumption.",
